> 3. Because the program stores the *source* IP and port in a global
>    array, a malicious actor could saturate the table by sending many
>    distinct packets, causing a denial‑of‑service scenario for the
>    parent’s printing routine.  
> 4. The code uses `255.255.255.255` as the broadcast address.  On some
>    operating systems this will fail unless the socket is explicitly
>    allowed to send broadcasts (`SO_BROADCAST`).  It also requires that
