3.   Collects and prints the **cache‑hit ratio** and the **average query delay** after a warm‑up period.  
4.   Produces one line per scenario – a CSV that can be plotted with any tool (e.g. gnuplot, Excel).  

> **How to use**  
> Compile with `gcc -O2 -lm -o cache_sim cache_sim.c`  
> Run with `./cache_sim` – the program will output a CSV file called `results.csv` and also print the values on stdout.  

