| 6 | **`scanf` return values are ignored**. | If the user enters non‑numeric input, the program behaves unpredictably. |
| 7 | **`float average = j / n;` uses integer division** (since `j` is `int`). | The average will be truncated. |
| 8 | **No bounds checking on `scanf` for the burst times**. | Malicious or accidental input can overflow `p[i].bursttime` (though it’s an `int` – still a risk). |
| 9 | **No input validation for negative or zero burst times**. | SJF assumes positive burst times; negative values would break the logic. |

