The algorithm is **deterministic Miller–Rabin** with a fixed set of bases that is proven to be correct for all numbers < 2⁶⁴.  
It is the fastest method that still runs in O(log n) time and works for any 64‑bit input (including 10¹⁸‑ish values).  
If you only need to test numbers up to a few million you can fall back to the simple `sqrt` check – I keep both versions so you can pick what fits your constraints.

