The code uses an integer‑only version of the **Newton–Raphson (Babylonian)** method, which is fast, easy to understand, and free from floating‑point rounding errors.  
I also included a brief discussion of common security pitfalls (integer overflow, unchecked input, etc.) so that a “security‑researcher‑mindset” is maintained.

