| **No buffer over‑runs** | Fixed‑size buffers (`MAX_LINE`) and careful use of `strlen()`/`strncat()`. |
| **No signed‑overflow** | All arithmetic is on `double` – no unchecked integer math. |
| **Safe string handling** | `snprintf()` (C99) and `strcat_s` (Windows) for concatenation. |
| **Error handling** | Every function return is checked and an informative message is printed. |

> **⚠️** This is **demo code**.  
> In production you’d want a more robust search (e.g. dynamic programming for arbitrary combinations), better tolerance handling, and a proper GUI or driver interface.  

