### 6.2 Authentication & Authorization

| Feature | Recommendation |
|---------|-----------------|
| **Login** | Enforce salted, hashed passwords (PBKDF2, Argon2). Store only the hash. |
| **Session Token** | Use a signed, random UUID with expiration (e.g., 30 min). |
| **Role Check** | Separate “user” and “agent” roles. Agent cannot upload arbitrary files; only authorized file types accepted. |
| **CSRF / Replay Protection** | Include nonce per session; validate on each request. |

### 6.3 Input Validation & Sanitization

| Data | Validation |
|------|------------|
| Text chat | Strip control chars, limit length (e.g., 2000 bytes). Escape HTML if rendering in `JEditorPane`. |
| Image | Verify MIME type (`ImageIO.read` returns non‑null). Reject non‑JPG/PNG. |
| File | Enforce whitelist: `.txt`, `.pdf`, `.jpg`, `.png`. Limit size (e.g., 5 MB). |
| File names | Normalize path (`Paths.get(fileName).normalize()`), reject absolute paths, ensure under a dedicated storage dir. |
| Commands | Define a strict protocol; drop unknown commands. |

### 6.4 File Storage & Persistence

| Concern | Mitigation |
|---------|------------|
| Log confidentiality | Encrypt logs with a symmetric key derived from a per‑user key (`AES‑GCM`). Store the key in a secure keystore. |
| Log integrity | Compute and store a hash (e.g., SHA‑256) per log entry; verify on load. |
| File upload directory | Separate per‑user folder under a locked root (`/srv/cs_files/`). Set proper OS permissions (`700`). |
