## 1. Overview of the export format

Jira can be exported as **XML** (classic export) or **JSON** (newer APIs).  
The example below parses the **XML** format because it is the most common one that contains:

```xml
<jira:jiraIssue>
  <jira:issue>
    <jira:issueKey>PROJECT-123</jira:issueKey>
    <jira:fields>
      <jira:summary>Some issue</jira:summary>
      <jira:description>Long description</jira:description>
      <jira:issuetype>
        <jira:name>Bug</jira:name>
      </jira:issuetype>
      <jira:status>
        <jira:name>Open</jira:name>
      </jira:status>
      <jira:created>2021-07-12T13:45:00.000+0000</jira:created>
      <jira:updated>2021-07-13T10:12:00.000+0000</jira:updated>
      <!-- … other fields … -->
    </jira:fields>
  </jira:issue>
</jira:jiraIssue>
