## 🛡️ Security Checklist (research‑level)

| Area | Recommendation | Rationale |
|------|----------------|-----------|
| **Password storage** | BCrypt (≥ 12 rounds) | Salting & slow hashing mitigates brute‑force. |
| **JWT secret** | ≥ 256 bits, stored in vault | Prevents token forging. |
| **Token lifetime** | Short (e.g. 15 min) + refresh token | Limits damage of compromised token. |
| **Refresh token** | HttpOnly, SameSite=Strict cookie | Reduces XSS & CSRF risk. |
| **Rate limiting** | 5‑10 reqs/min per IP/user | Stops automated brute‑force on login. |
| **Account lockout** | After N failed logins | Stops credential stuffing. |
| **Input validation** | `@Validated`, `@Email`, `@Size` | Avoids injection attacks. |
| **CORS** | Whitelist exact origins | Prevents CSRF via cross‑origin. |
| **HTTPS only** | Enforce TLS | Stops MITM, token theft. |
| **Audit logs** | Log auth events (success/failure) | Enables incident investigation. |
| **Token revocation list** | Optional DB/Redis blacklist | Allows immediate logout or key rotation. |

