The program also contains the usual safety checks you should expect when working with file I/O and user input.

> **Why this matters for security research**  
>  • Random selection that is *predictable* (`java.util.Random`) can be brute‑forced.  
>  • Reading a large file into RAM can expose you to a Denial‑of‑Service (DoS) via huge inputs.  
>  • Proper input validation (path traversal, file‑type checks) protects against accidental or malicious misuse.

