| **No global error mapping** | When an unhandled exception is thrown, Spring Boot falls back to the *Whitelabel* page. | Attackers can use the 500 to probe your application. | Add a `@ControllerAdvice` that maps `Exception.class` to a custom `error.html`, and optionally a `ErrorController` that logs the exception safely. |
| **Using the old MySQL driver class** | `com.mysql.jdbc.Driver` is deprecated; if the driver jar isn’t on the classpath the datasource fails to start → 500. | A missing driver can allow a DoS attack (app never starts). | Use `com.mysql.cj.jdbc.Driver` (or add the driver dependency explicitly). |
| **Hard‑coded credentials in `application.properties`** | Anyone who obtains `application.properties` (e.g., via a mis‑configured file‑system view or a backup) now has DB access. | Data breach. | Use environment variables or Spring Cloud Vault / AWS Secrets Manager. |
