## 2. Core Classes

### 2.1 `FileInfo`

```java
package com.example.fileindexer;

import com.fasterxml.jackson.annotation.JsonProperty;

public class FileInfo {
    @JsonProperty("path")
    public String path;
    @JsonProperty("size")
    public long size;
    @JsonProperty("lastModified")
    public long lastModified;
    @JsonProperty("hash")
    public String hash;     // optional; SHA‑256 of the file

    // Needed by Jackson
    public FileInfo() {}

    public FileInfo(String path, long size, long lastModified, String hash) {
        this.path = path;
        this.size = size;
        this.lastModified = lastModified;
        this.hash = hash;
    }
}
```

> *Why a hash?*  
> It lets you detect content changes even if timestamps are unchanged (e.g., when a file is “patched” in‑place).

