### 2.5 `Searcher`

A tiny helper that exposes a command‑line search interface.

```java
package com.example.fileindexer;

import java.util.*;

public class Searcher {
    private final FileIndex index;

    public Searcher(FileIndex index) { this.index = index; }

    public void interactiveSearch() {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.println("File Indexer – Search Mode");
        System.out.println("Enter file name fragment (or 'quit' to exit):");
        while (true) {
            System.out.print("> ");
            String query = sc.nextLine().trim();
            if ("quit".equalsIgnoreCase(query)) break;

            List<FileInfo> hits = new ArrayList<>(index.search(query));
            System.out.println("Found " + hits.size() + " matches:");
            for (FileInfo fi : hits) {
                System.out.printf("  %s (size=%d, modified=%tF %tT)\n",
                        fi.path, fi.size, new java.util.Date(fi.lastModified), new java.util.Date(fi.lastModified));
            }
        }
    }
}
```

