### 2.6 `Main`

Wire everything together.

```java
package com.example.fileindexer;

import java.nio.file.Path;
import java.nio.file.Paths;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Path idxFile = Paths.get(System.getProperty("user.home"), ".file_index.json");
        FileIndex index = new FileIndex(idxFile);

        // 1️⃣  Index everything if the index file is empty or non‑existent
        if (index.search("").isEmpty()) {
            System.out.println("[+] Performing initial full scan – this may take a while.");
            Indexer indexer = new Indexer(index);
            indexer.indexAllDrives();
        }

        // 2️⃣  Start the change‑watcher in its own thread
        try {
            Thread watcherThread = new Thread(new FileWatcher(index), "FileWatcher");
            watcherThread.setDaemon(true);
            watcherThread.start();
        } catch (Exception e) {
            System.err.println("[!] Could not start watcher: " + e.getMessage());
        }

        // 3️⃣  Simple command line search
        Searcher searcher = new Searcher(index);
        searcher.interactiveSearch();

        // 4️⃣  Save the index before exiting
        index.save();
