## 2. Define the “Task” contract

```java
// 1️⃣  Task.java  (common module, compiled into a JAR and used by both sides)
package com.example.distrib;

import java.io.Serializable;
import java.util.concurrent.Callable;

public interface Task<T> extends Serializable, Callable<T> {
    // `call()` is the work that will be executed remotely
    @Override
    T call() throws Exception;
}
```

*All tasks must be `Serializable` because we’ll stream them over sockets.*  
*By extending `Callable<T>` we automatically get a return value.*

> **Example task** – a simple prime‑number sieve that runs on the worker:

```java
// 2️⃣  PrimeTask.java
package com.example.distrib;

public class PrimeTask implements Task<Boolean> {
    private static final long serialVersionUID = 1L;
    private final int number;

    public PrimeTask(int number) {
        this.number = number;
    }

    @Override
    public Boolean call() {
        if (number < 2) return false;
        for (int i = 2; i <= Math.sqrt(number); i++) {
            if (number % i == 0) return false;
        }
        return true;
    }
}
```

Compile this JAR once and put it in the *common* project folder (or use a shared Gradle/Maven dependency).

