        ClientHandler(Socket s, int id) throws IOException {
            this.socket = s;
            this.id = id;
            this.in  = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(socket.getInputStream()));
            this.out = new PrintWriter(new BufferedWriter(new OutputStreamWriter(socket.getOutputStream())), true);
            // Send initial symbol
            out.println(symbols[id]); // 'X' or 'O'
        }

        public void run() {
            try {
                String line;
                while ((line = in.readLine()) != null) {
                    Move move = mapper.readValue(line, Move.class);
                    if (move.symbol != symbols[currentTurn]) {
                        out.println("ERROR: Not your turn");
                        continue;
                    }
                    if (!board.applyMove(move.row, move.col, move.symbol)) {
                        out.println("ERROR: Invalid move");
                        continue;
                    }
                    broadcastMove(move);
                    checkGame(move);
                    currentTurn = 1 - currentTurn;
                }
            } catch (IOException e) {
                System.err.println("Client " + id + " disconnected");
            } finally {
                try { socket.close(); } catch (IOException ignore) {}
            }
        }

        void send(Move m) throws IOException {
            out.println(mapper.writeValueAsString(m));
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {
        new Server().start();
    }
}
```

> **What’s happening?**  
> * Two `ClientHandler`s are created for two connections.  
> * Moves are validated on the server.  
> * After each valid move, the server broadcasts to both clients.  
> * Simple “turn” logic ensures players alternate.  

