### 3.4. MessageBuilder (common helper)

```java
package com.ecommerce.chat.common;

import javax.json.Json;
import javax.json.JsonObject;
import java.security.GeneralSecurityException;

public class MessageBuilder {
    public static JsonObject roleAnnounce(String role, String id) throws GeneralSecurityException {
        JsonObject body = Json.createObjectBuilder()
                .add("role", role)
                .add(role, id)
                .build();
        return sign(body);
    }

    public static JsonObject textMsg(String sessionId, int seq, String text) throws GeneralSecurityException {
        JsonObject body = Json.createObjectBuilder()
                .add("type", "text")
                .add("sessionId", sessionId)
                .add("seq", seq)
                .add("text", text)
                .build();
        return sign(body);
    }

    public static JsonObject fileMsg(String sessionId, int seq, String fname, String data, String mime) throws GeneralSecurityException {
        JsonObject body = Json.createObjectBuilder()
                .add("type", "file")
                .add("sessionId", sessionId)
                .add("seq", seq)
                .add("fileName", fname)
                .add("mime", mime)
                .add("data", data)
                .build();
        return sign(body);
    }

    private static JsonObject sign(JsonObject body) throws GeneralSecurityException {
        byte[] raw = CryptoUtil.jsonToBytes(body);
        String hmac = CryptoUtil.computeHmac(raw);
        return Json.createObjectBuilder(body).add("hmac", hmac).build();
    }
}
```

> **Why this builder?**  
> The `sign` method adds an HMAC to every outgoing message, ensuring that the server can verify authenticity and that the message cannot be tampered with in transit.

