| Issue | Why it matters | Fix |
|-------|----------------|-----|
| **Plaintext traffic** | Anyone on the same network can eavesdrop | Wrap sockets in TLS (`SSLServerSocket`, `SSLSocket`) and use certificates. |
| **No authentication** | An attacker can join the chat and flood it | Require a username/password or token; validate on the server. |
| **Unbounded input** | A client could send an enormous line and exhaust memory | Enforce a maximum line length, e.g., read `BufferedReader.readLine()` but reject if > 4 kB. |
