## 4. Security‑specific notes

| Feature | Implementation sketch | Why it matters |
|---------|-----------------------|----------------|
| **Transport encryption** | Wrap `Socket` in an `SSLSocket` using a self‑signed cert or a CA cert. | Prevents eavesdropping & tampering. |
| **Rate‑limiting** | Use `RateLimiter` (Guava) per IP or per client to block floods. | Defends against DoS. |
| **Replay protection** | Issue a random session token per connection; require the token in every command (e.g., `vote N <token>`). | Stops a captured command from being replayed. |
