Below is a **complete, self‑contained example** that shows how you can build a simple RMI service that

1. Generates a 300‑word “encyclopedia” of random data.  
2. Exposes the five required functions with the **exact names** you asked for.  
3. Lets a Swing GUI client invoke those functions **sequentially** (non‑threaded) and **in parallel** (multi‑threaded) so you can measure the elapsed time and calculate the speed‑up.

> **NOTE** – The code is written for Java 17+ (any Java 8 or later will work).  
> The RMI service is intentionally **un‑secured** – don’t expose it on an untrusted network.

---

## 1.  The RMI Interface

```java
// File: DataService.java
import java.rmi.Remote;
import java.rmi.RemoteException;

public interface DataService extends Remote {

    // 1‑letter count (spaces included)
    int Count() throws RemoteException;

    // 2‑repeated words (comma separated)
    String repeatedwords() throws RemoteException;

    // 3‑longest word
    String longest() throws RemoteException;

    // 4‑shortest word
    String shortest() throws RemoteException;

    // 5‑repeat‑count map (word:count, …)
    String Repeat() throws RemoteException;
}
```

> **Why `String` for the return values?**  
> `String` is serialisable and avoids exposing internal data structures to the client.

---

## 2.  The Server Implementation

```java
// File: DataServiceImpl.java
import java.rmi.RemoteException;
import java.rmi.server.UnicastRemoteObject;
import java.util.*;

public class DataServiceImpl extends UnicastRemoteObject implements DataService {

    private static final long serialVersionUID = 1L;
    private final List<String> words;
    private final Map<String, Integer> freqMap;
    private final int totalLettersIncludingSpaces;

    protected DataServiceImpl() throws RemoteException {
        super();
        this.words = generateWords(300);
        this.freqMap = computeFrequencies(words);
        this.totalLettersIncludingSpaces = calculateTotalLength(words);
    }

    // ---------- 5 required methods ----------
    @Override
    public int Count() {
        return totalLettersIncludingSpaces;
    }

    @Override
    public String repeatedwords() {
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        for (Map.Entry<String, Integer> e : freqMap.entrySet()) {
            if (e.getValue() > 1) {
                if (sb.length() > 0) sb.append(", ");
                sb.append(e.getKey());
            }
        }
        return sb.toString();
    }

    @Override
    public String longest() {
        String longest = "";
        for (String w : words) {
            if (w.length() > longest.length()) longest = w;
        }
        return longest;
    }

    @Override
    public String shortest() {
        String shortest = null;
        for (String w : words) {
            if (shortest == null || w.length() < shortest.length()) shortest = w;
        }
        return shortest;
    }

    @Override
    public String Repeat() {
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        for (Map.Entry<String, Integer> e : freqMap.entrySet()) {
            if (sb.length() > 0) sb.append(", ");
            sb.append(e.getKey()).append(":").append(e.getValue());
        }
        return sb.toString();
    }

    // ---------- helper methods ----------
    private List<String> generateWords(int count) {
        Random rnd = new Random(12345);   // deterministic seed for reproducibility
        List<String> list = new ArrayList<>(count);
        for (int i = 0; i < count; i++) {
            int len = rnd.nextInt(10) + 3;          // 3‑12 letters
            StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder(len);
            for (int j = 0; j < len; j++) {
                sb.append((char) ('a' + rnd.nextInt(26)));
            }
            list.add(sb.toString());
        }
        return list;
    }

    private Map<String, Integer> computeFrequencies(List<String> ws) {
        Map<String, Integer> map = new HashMap<>();
        for (String w : ws) {
            map.merge(w, 1, Integer::sum);
        }
        return map;
    }

    private int calculateTotalLength(List<String> ws) {
        int total = 0;
        for (String w : ws) total += w.length();
        // + spaces between words
        total += ws.size() - 1;
        return total;
    }
}
```

> **Deterministic seed** – this makes the random data reproducible across runs, which is handy when comparing single‑threaded vs. multi‑threaded timings.

---

## 3.  RMI Registry / Server Starter

```java
// File: Server.java
import java.rmi.registry.LocateRegistry;
import java.rmi.registry.Registry;
import java.rmi.server.UnicastRemoteObject;

public class Server {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            DataServiceImpl impl = new DataServiceImpl();

            // Export the remote object
            DataService stub = (DataService) UnicastRemoteObject.exportObject(impl, 0);

            // Bind it to the name "DataService"
            Registry registry = LocateRegistry.createRegistry(1099); // default port
            registry.rebind("DataService", stub);

            System.out.println("Server ready – waiting for client calls...");
        } catch (Exception e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
}
