| Feature | Why it matters |
|---------|----------------|
| **`withCredentials: true`** | Sends HttpOnly cookie (access token). Prevents XSS stealing the token. |
| **CSRF token header** | Protects against cross‑site request forgery if you also set `SameSite=Strict` or `SameSite=Lax`. |
| **Timeout + maxContentLength** | Stops malicious or buggy servers from hanging the UI or sending huge payloads. |
| **Global error handling** | Central point for logout, token refresh, audit logs. |
| **Retry logic** | Handles transient network errors without exposing raw network noise to the user. |
| **No `eval`, no inline scripts** | The client never injects untrusted data into the DOM – React’s virtual DOM and JSX already protect against XSS. |
| **Environment variable for base URL** | Keeps the production API endpoint out of source control. |
| **No console secrets** | The code never logs any token or secret to the browser console. |

