});
```

> **How to run**
> ```bash
> npm init -y           # (if you haven’t created a package.json yet)
> npm install express
> node index.js
> ```

---

## 2️⃣ index.html – Client Page

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>BPM Detector</title>
  <style>
    body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; text-align: center; margin-top: 4rem; }
    #bpm { font-size: 3rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
    #status { margin-top: 1rem; color: #666; }
    button { font-size: 1rem; padding: 0.5rem 1rem; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

<h1>Live BPM Detector</h1>
<button id="startBtn">Start Listening</button>
<div id="status">Awaiting user permission...</div>
<div id="bpm"></div>

<script>
const startBtn = document.getElementById('startBtn');
const statusEl = document.getElementById('status');
const bpmEl = document.getElementById('bpm');

let audioCtx;
let analyser;
let dataArray;
let bufferLength;
let lastPeakTime = 0;
let peakTimes = [];
let bpm = 0;

// Simple peak detection parameters
const PEAK_THRESHOLD = 0.6;  // Adjust depending on audio level
const MIN_PEAK_INTERVAL = 200; // ms, to avoid detecting the same beat twice

startBtn.addEventListener('click', async () => {
  if (!navigator.mediaDevices || !navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia) {
    statusEl.textContent = 'getUserMedia not supported on your browser.';
    return;
  }

  try {
    const stream = await navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia({ audio: true });
    audioCtx = new (window.AudioContext || window.webkitAudioContext)();
    const source = audioCtx.createMediaStreamSource(stream);

    analyser = audioCtx.createAnalyser();
    analyser.fftSize = 2048;
    bufferLength = analyser.fftSize;
    dataArray = new Uint8Array(bufferLength);

    source.connect(analyser);

    statusEl.textContent = 'Listening…';
    startBtn.disabled = true;

    analyzeAudio();
  } catch (err) {
    console.error(err);
    statusEl.textContent = 'Microphone access denied.';
  }
});

function analyzeAudio() {
  analyser.getByteTimeDomainData(dataArray);

  // Convert byte array (0-255) to float (-1 to 1)
  let sum = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < bufferLength; i++) {
    const val = dataArray[i] / 128 - 1; // 0–255 → –1–1
    sum += val * val; // Energy
  }
  const rms = Math.sqrt(sum / bufferLength);

  const now = performance.now();

  // Detect a peak if rms exceeds threshold and enough time has passed
  if (rms > PEAK_THRESHOLD && now - lastPeakTime > MIN_PEAK_INTERVAL) {
    lastPeakTime = now;
    peakTimes.push(now);

    // Keep only the last ~20 peaks (about 2–3 seconds)
    if (peakTimes.length > 20) peakTimes.shift();

    // Compute BPM from the intervals between successive peaks
    if (peakTimes.length >= 2) {
      const intervals = [];
      for (let i = 1; i < peakTimes.length; i++) {
        intervals.push(peakTimes[i] - peakTimes[i - 1]); // ms
      }
      // Average interval
      const avgInterval = intervals.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / intervals.length;
      bpm = Math.round(60000 / avgInterval); // 60,000 ms per minute
      bpmEl.textContent = bpm + ' BPM';
    }
  }

  requestAnimationFrame(analyzeAudio);
}
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

---

### How it Works

1. **Microphone Access** – The user clicks the button → `navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia({ audio: true })`.
2. **Audio Capture** – We create an `AudioContext` and feed the microphone stream into an `AnalyserNode`.
3. **Peak Detection** – In each animation frame, we compute the root‑mean‑square (RMS) energy of the time‑domain buffer.  
   When the RMS exceeds a threshold **and** enough time has elapsed since the last detected peak, we consider that a beat.
4. **BPM Calculation** – We keep an array of recent peak timestamps, compute the differences (intervals) between successive peaks, average those intervals, and convert to BPM (`60000 / avgInterval`).
5. **Display** – The BPM value updates live in the page.

> **Tuning**  
> - `PEAK_THRESHOLD`: Increase if you’re not detecting beats (e.g., due to low volume), decrease if you’re getting false positives.  
> - `MIN_PEAK_INTERVAL`: Helps avoid counting the same beat twice, especially for very fast tempos.

---

### Quick Test

1. Save the two files (`index.js` and `index.html`) in the same folder.
2. Run `node index.js` from that folder.
3. Open your browser at `http://localhost:3000/`.
4. Click **Start Listening**, then play a rhythmic track (metronome, drum loop, etc.) through the microphone.  
   The BPM will appear in real time.

---

Enjoy experimenting with it! Feel free to tweak the thresholds or replace the simple RMS‑based detection with a more sophisticated spectral‑flux or onset‑detector algorithm if you need higher accuracy.

