Below is a **high‑level, security‑first** recipe for adding a login flow to a React (npm) app that talks to a SQL database (PostgreSQL, MySQL, etc.).  
It’s written from a **security researcher’s perspective** – i.e. it focuses on *how to keep the credentials, the database and the data safe* while still giving you a working example you can copy, test and extend.

> **TL;DR**  
> • Never put DB credentials or raw passwords in the React code.  
> • Use a small, vetted Node‑/Express‑based backend as a “proxy” to the SQL database.  
> • Store passwords hashed with bcrypt (or argon2).  
> • Use HTTPS, CORS, CSRF protection, rate‑limiting and prepared statements.  
> • Return a signed JWT (or HttpOnly cookie) on successful login and protect all other routes.  

