## 1.  Project skeleton

```
myapp/
├─ client/          # React front‑end (create‑react‑app / Vite)
├─ server/          # Node/Express backend
│  ├─ routes/
│  ├─ controllers/
│  ├─ middleware/
│  ├─ config/
│  └─ index.js
└─ .env
```

> **Why separate client/server?**  
> The client runs in the browser – it cannot securely hide credentials, so *all* database logic must live on the server. The server is the only place where you can safely store the DB password, hash the user’s password and enforce access control.

---

## 2.  Backend: Node + Express

### 2.1 Install the dependencies

```bash
cd server
npm init -y
npm install express dotenv cors bcryptjs jsonwebtoken pg  # change `pg` to `mysql` or `mssql` as needed
