It contains the three Russian name fields you asked for – *Фамилия*, *Имя*, *Отчество* – and demonstrates how to handle them in a safe way.

| Feature | Why it matters for security |
|---------|----------------------------|
| **Strong typing** (`React.FC<...>`, `FormData`) | Prevents accidental misuse of data and reduces injection vectors. |
| **Controlled inputs** | Guarantees that the component owns the data and you can run validation before submission. |
| **Client‑side validation** | Stops obvious mistakes early, but does *not* replace server‑side validation. |
| **No direct string interpolation into the DOM** | Prevents XSS by letting React do the escaping. |
| **CSRF protection** (`axios` with `withCredentials` + server‑side token) | Stops cross‑site request forgery. |
| **HTTPS + secure headers** | Make sure your API endpoint uses TLS; the sample uses `https://api.example.com/...`. |
| **Rate‑limiting & input sanitization** | Server‑side best practice, but you can add simple checks here. |
| **No sensitive data stored in local storage** | Keeps user data in memory only until the request completes. |

> **Tip**: Always remember that *client‑side* checks are only a first line of defense. The **server** must re‑validate all input and guard against XSS, CSRF, injection, etc.

---

## 1️⃣  Project Setup (quick start)

```bash
npx create-react-app secure-form-ts --template typescript
cd secure-form-ts
npm install axios
```

Replace the contents of `src/App.tsx` with the code below.

---

## 2️⃣  The Form Component (src/App.tsx)

```tsx
import React, { useState, FormEvent } from 'react';
import axios from 'axios';

/** 1. Strongly‑typed form data */
interface FormData {
  фамилия: string;
  имя: string;
  отчество: string;
}

/** 2. Helper to trim & check emptiness */
const isEmpty = (s: string) => !s.trim();

/** 3. Main component */
const App: React.FC = () => {
  // 3a. State: holds the form values
  const [values, setValues] = useState<FormData>({
    фамилия: '',
    имя: '',
    отчество: '',
  });

  // 3b. State: holds validation errors
  const [errors, setErrors] = useState<Partial<Record<keyof FormData, string>>>({});

  // 3c. State: shows success/failure
  const [status, setStatus] = useState<null | 'success' | 'error'>(null);

  /** 4. Generic change handler */
  const handleChange = (e: React.ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>) => {
    const { name, value } = e.target;
    setValues(prev => ({ ...prev, [name]: value }));
  };

  /** 5. Client‑side validation */
  const validate = (): boolean => {
    const newErrors: Partial<Record<keyof FormData, string>> = {};

    if (isEmpty(values.фамилия)) newErrors.фамилия = 'Фамилия обязательна';
    if (isEmpty(values.имя))     newErrors.имя     = 'Имя обязательно';
    if (isEmpty(values.отчество)) newErrors.отчество = 'Отчество обязательно';

    // Optional: restrict characters (only Cyrillic, spaces, hyphens)
    const cyrillicPattern = /^[\u0400-\u04FF\s-]+$/;
    ['фамилия', 'имя', 'отчество'].forEach(field => {
      if (
        values[field as keyof FormData] &&
        !cyrillicPattern.test(values[field as keyof FormData])
      ) {
        newErrors[field as keyof FormData] = 'Только кириллица, пробелы, дефис';
      }
    });

    setErrors(newErrors);
    return Object.keys(newErrors).length === 0;
  };

  /** 6. Submit handler */
  const handleSubmit = async (e: FormEvent) => {
    e.preventDefault();           // Stop default form post

    if (!validate()) return;      // Bail if client‑side checks fail

    try {
      // 6a. Send data securely (HTTPS + CSRF token if required)
      await axios.post(
        'https://api.example.com/v1/submit',
        { ...values },                 // Send as JSON
        {
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
          withCredentials: true,        // Sends cookies (CSRF token) if needed
        }
      );
      setStatus('success');
    } catch (err: any) {
      console.error(err);
      setStatus('error');
    }
  };

  return (
    <div style={{ maxWidth: 400, margin: '2rem auto', fontFamily: 'Arial, sans-serif' }}>
      <h2>Регистрация пользователя</h2>

      <form onSubmit={handleSubmit} noValidate>
        {/* Фамилия */}
        <div style={{ marginBottom: 12 }}>
          <label htmlFor="фамилия" style={{ display: 'block' }}>
            Фамилия *
          </label>
          <input
            id="фамилия"
            name="фамилия"
            type="text"
            value={values.фамилия}
            onChange={handleChange}
            autoComplete="family-name"
            aria-invalid={!!errors.фамилия}
            aria-describedby="фамилия-error"
            required
          />
          {errors.фамилия && (
            <span id="фамилия-error" style={{ color: 'red' }}>
              {errors.фамилия}
            </span>
          )}
        </div>

        {/* Имя */}
        <div style={{ marginBottom: 12 }}>
          <label htmlFor="имя" style={{ display: 'block' }}>
            Имя *
          </label>
          <input
            id="имя"
            name="имя"
            type="text"
            value={values.имя}
            onChange={handleChange}
            autoComplete="given-name"
            aria-invalid={!!errors.имя}
            aria-describedby="имя-error"
            required
          />
          {errors.имя && (
            <span id="имя-error" style={{ color: 'red' }}>
              {errors.имя}
            </span>
          )}
        </div>

        {/* Отчество */}
        <div style={{ marginBottom: 12 }}>
          <label htmlFor="отчество" style={{ display: 'block' }}>
            Отчество *
          </label>
          <input
            id="отчество"
            name="отчество"
            type="text"
            value={values.отчество}
            onChange={handleChange}
            autoComplete="additional-name"
            aria-invalid={!!errors.отчество}
            aria-describedby="отчество-error"
            required
          />
          {errors.отчество && (
            <span id="отчество-error" style={{ color: 'red' }}>
              {errors.отчество}
            </span>
          )}
        </div>

        <button type="submit">Отправить</button>
      </form>

      {/* Feedback */}
      {status === 'success' && (
        <p style={{ color: 'green', marginTop: 12 }}>
          Данные успешно отправлены!
        </p>
      )}
      {status === 'error' && (
        <p style={{ color: 'red', marginTop: 12 }}>
          Ошибка при отправке. Попробуйте ещё раз.
        </p>
      )}
    </div>
  );
};

export default App;
```

---

## 3️⃣  What the Code Does (security‑oriented)

1. **TypeScript guarantees** that the `FormData` shape is correct everywhere.
2. **Controlled inputs** give us full control over user data before it ever reaches the network.
3. **Validation** runs in the browser, but is only a first filter— the server *must* duplicate all checks.
4. **Regular expressions** limit the allowed character set, cutting down the risk of script injection.
5. **`axios.post`** sends a JSON payload over HTTPS.  
   - `withCredentials: true` includes cookies (useful for CSRF tokens).  
   - The `Content-Type` header is set explicitly to avoid MIME‑type confusion.
6. **Error handling** logs the error to the console (for dev) and gives user‑friendly feedback without leaking sensitive data.
7. **No sensitive data is stored** in local storage or cookies on the client side.  
   If you need persistence, encrypt before storing or rely on secure server‑side sessions.

---

## 4️⃣  Server‑Side Checklist (not part of the client code)

| Item | Why |
|------|-----|
| **HTTPS everywhere** | Protects data in transit. |
| **CSRF token validation** | Prevents cross‑site request forgery. |
| **Input sanitization & escaping** | Stops XSS, injection, and data corruption. |
| **Rate‑limit endpoints** | Mitigates brute‑force and DoS attempts. |
| **Logging & monitoring** | Detects abuse and attacks early. |
| **Least‑privilege data handling** | Store only necessary fields; avoid logging PII. |

---

### Done!

You now have a fully typed, secure, and user‑friendly form component that you can drop into any React/TypeScript project. Adjust the endpoint URL, add authentication headers, or integrate with your existing API as needed.

