Below is a “security‑first” walk‑through for **deleting a lobby (or any Colyseus room) once the game ends**.  
It covers:

| What you need | Why it matters | Typical Colyseus pattern |
|---------------|----------------|--------------------------|
| **Authoritative validation** of the end‑state | Prevents a malicious client from faking “game over” | Server‑side flag / hash |
| **Strict access control** to the `dispose()` call | Only the game logic / host should trigger deletion | Role‑based checks |
| **Race‑safe cleanup** (no dangling timers, events, DB rows) | Avoid memory leaks and data leakage | `onDispose`/`onLeave` |
| **Graceful disconnect** of players | Ensures all clients know the lobby is gone | Broadcast + force disconnect |
| **Idempotency & logging** | Re‑tries or accidental double deletes won’t corrupt state | Idempotent dispose logic |
| **Resource revocation** (e.g. DB TTL, Redis keys) | Removes stale game state | TTL on persistence |
| **Secure cleanup of global registries** | Avoid stale lobby references | `removeRoom` or global map cleanup |

---

## 1.  The “lobby” vs “game” room

- **LobbyRoom** – waiting area for players, usually `< 2` players, may have a short `idleTimeout`.
- **GameRoom** – actual game logic, holds state, runs until game‑over condition.

You can keep the two separate, or treat the lobby as a transient `GameRoom` that immediately deletes itself once all players are ready.

---

## 2.  Example – “GameRoom” that deletes itself

```ts
// src/rooms/GameRoom.ts
import { Room, Client, Server } from "colyseus";

export default class GameRoom extends Room {
  // Called once when the room is created
  onCreate(options: any) {
    // Security: require a signed “host” token for starting the game
    // (e.g. options.hostToken verified elsewhere)
    this.setState(new GameState()); // <-- your game state schema

    // Set idle timeout for safety: if no clients after 5 mins, dispose
    this.setIdleTimeout(300_000);

    // Listen for a special "gameOver" message from the server logic
    this.onMessage("gameOver", () => {
      this.endGame();
    });

    // Optional: log when the room is created
    console.log(`[GameRoom ${this.roomId}] created by host`, this.hostClientId);
  }

  // Called when any client joins
  onJoin(client: Client, options: any) {
    console.log(`[GameRoom ${this.roomId}] client ${client.sessionId} joined`);
  }

  // Called when any client leaves
  onLeave(client: Client, consented: boolean) {
    console.log(`[GameRoom ${this.roomId}] client ${client.sessionId} left`);
    // If the host leaves, you could decide to end the game early
    if (client.sessionId === this.hostClientId) this.endGame(true);
  }

  // ---- Game logic ----

  // Example game over trigger, could be called by the server logic
  private endGame(earlyLeave = false) {
    // 1. Verify that the game really finished on the server side
    //    (e.g., check a hash or a server‑side flag)
    if (!this.isGameFinished()) {
      console.warn(`[GameRoom ${this.roomId}] aborting dispose: game not finished`);
      return;
    }

    // 2. Notify clients that the game is over
    this.broadcast("gameEnd", { reason: earlyLeave ? "host left" : "normal" });

    // 3. Gracefully disconnect clients *after* broadcast
    //    (you can also skip disconnecting if you want the browser to stay connected)
    this.clients.forEach((c) => {
      // send final state before closing
      c.send("finalState", this.state);
      // optionally: c.disconnect(); // force close
    });

    // 4. Cleanup any timers or external resources
    this.cleanupExternalResources();

    // 5. Finally, dispose the room – this removes it from Colyseus
    //    and triggers onDispose below.  It is safe to call even
    //    if some clients are still in flight.
    this.dispose();
  }

  // Example validation – make sure the game is truly finished
  private isGameFinished(): boolean {
    // For example: check a flag that the server set when the final score was computed
    return this.state.gameOver === true;
  }

  // Clean up any external resources (Redis keys, DB rows, timers)
  private cleanupExternalResources() {
    // e.g., clear a Redis key that holds the lobby ID
    // await this.server.redis.del(`lobby:${this.roomId}`);
    // clear timers
    clearInterval(this.someInterval);
  }

  // Called once right before the room is removed from memory
  onDispose() {
    console.log(`[GameRoom ${this.roomId}] disposed`);
    // Remove any global lobby registry entries
    // Example: globalLobbyMap.delete(this.roomId);
    // Also emit to admin dashboards if needed
  }
}
```

### Key points in the code

| Line | Purpose | Security benefit |
|------|---------|------------------|
| `this.setIdleTimeout(300_000)` | Auto‑dispose after 5 min idle | Prevents orphan rooms |
| `onMessage("gameOver")` | Server‑driven trigger | Client cannot fake |
| `isGameFinished()` | Server‑side validation | No client‑side trust |
| `this.broadcast("gameEnd")` | Notify all players | Prevents “ghost” lobby |
| `this.dispose()` | Explicit room removal | Ensures `onDispose` runs |
| `onDispose()` | Final cleanup | Guarantees no leaks |

