## 1. Quick‑look “what changes are needed”

| What | Why |
|------|-----|
| `app.listen(3000, () => …)` → `app.listen(process.env.PORT || 80, '0.0.0.0')` | Bind to *all* interfaces (public‑visible) and allow the cloud provider to pick the port. |
| Add **HTTPS** (or let a reverse‑proxy handle TLS) | Prevent eavesdropping and MITM. |
| Store **hashed** passwords | Never keep passwords in plain text. |
| Use `helmet` for common headers | Mitigate click‑jacking, XSS, etc. |
| Validate & sanitize inputs | Avoid injection and bad data. |
| Rate‑limit & CSRF protection | Prevent brute‑force & CSRF attacks. |
| Serve files from a **public** bucket or CDN | Offload static assets and improve performance. |
| Log *only* necessary information | Keep logs useful but not a data source for attackers. |

