## 4. Security checklist (quick audit)

| ✅ | Item | Why |
|----|------|-----|
| ✅ | Passwords hashed (bcrypt) | Prevent credential theft |
| ✅ | Helmet headers | Reduce XSS, click‑jacking, MIME sniffing |
| ✅ | CSRF token & secure session cookies | Prevent cross‑site request forgery |
| ✅ | Rate limiting | Thwart brute‑force |
| ✅ | Input validation & sanitization | Avoid injection & malformed data |
| ✅ | HTTPS (or TLS termination at reverse‑proxy) | Protect data in transit |
| ✅ | No sensitive data in logs | Avoid leaking secrets |
| ✅ | Secrets via environment variables | Keep credentials out of code |

**Tip:** Add `npm audit` and `snyk` scanning to your CI pipeline.

---

## 5. Next steps for a security‑first mindset

1. **Use a database** (PostgreSQL, MongoDB, etc.) instead of a flat `users.json`.  
2. **Add password reset flow** with email OTP or magic link.  
3. **Implement account lockout** after a set number of failed logins.  
