Below is a **minimal, self‑contained fix** that

* keeps the caret‑animation working even when you type very fast or resize the window  
* prevents “stuck” blocks or empty space under the textarea  
* removes the *“highlightedLine is null”* error  
* does not rely on backticks (so you can paste it straight into the UI)

The idea is:

| Problem | Fix |
|---------|-----|
| Every `keydown` creates a **new** `<span>` and a new timer → timers pile up | Keep *one* highlight element only; clear any existing timers before starting a new one |
| `updateTimeout()` clears `animationTimeout` **after** calling `requestAnimationFrame()` → the animation is never seen | Use `setTimeout()` with the exact duration of the animation – that guarantees the element disappears after the animation ends |
| `onAnimationEnd()` runs even if there is no highlight (e.g. during a resize) → `highlightedLine` is `null` | Guard against a missing element |
| Inserting `<br>` before the caret pushes the caret to a new line **and** adds vertical space | Insert the caret *after* the `<br>` but never add an extra `<br>` – the caret itself is a block‑level element that occupies no extra height |

---

## 1️⃣ HTML

```html
<div id="editor" class="container" contenteditable="true"></div>
```

> *Use a `contenteditable` `<div>` (not a `<textarea>`).  This is what the original code was expecting.*

---

## 2️⃣ CSS – the blinking caret

```css
.container {
  font: 16px/1.5 monospace;
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 800px;
  min-height: 200px;
  border: 1px solid #ccc;
  padding: 8px;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  overflow-wrap: break-word;
  white-space: pre-wrap;
}

.highlight-line {
  display: inline-block;            /* makes it behave like a character */
  background: none;
  color: transparent;               /* hide the “█” during animation */
  animation: blink 1s linear infinite;
}

@keyframes blink {
  0%, 50% { opacity: 1; }
  51%, 100% { opacity: 0; }
}
```

> *The animation is purely visual; the element itself has no width.  We change its `animation-duration` in JS to make it “jump” to the right.*

---

## 3️⃣ JavaScript

```js
/* -------------  Global state ------------- */
const editor = document.getElementById('editor');

let updateTimer   = null;   // debounce the calculation after each key
let removeTimer   = null;   // timeout that removes the caret after animation

/* -------------  Core helpers ------------- */
function getCaretNode() {
  const sel = window.getSelection();
  if (!sel.rangeCount) return null;
  const range = sel.getRangeAt(0);
  return range.startContainer;
}

function createCaret() {
  const caret = document.createElement('span');
  caret.className = 'highlight-line';
  caret.textContent = '█';           // visible during animation
  return caret;
}

/* -------------  Insert a line (Enter) ------------- */
function insertLine() {
  const sel = window.getSelection();
  if (!sel.rangeCount) return;
  const range = sel.getRangeAt(0);

  // split the text node at the caret so we can insert the line break
  const node = range.startContainer;
  if (node.nodeType !== Node.TEXT_NODE) return;

  const offset = range.startOffset;
  const afterNode = node.splitText(offset);

  // create a <br> that will be the new line
  const br = document.createElement('br');

  // insert <br> and the caret after the split text
  afterNode.parentNode.insertBefore(br, afterNode);
  afterNode.parentNode.insertBefore(createCaret(), afterNode);

  // put the caret after the <br>
  range.setStart(afterNode, 0);
  range.collapse(true);
  sel.removeAllRanges();
  sel.addRange(range);

  scheduleUpdate();
}

/* -------------  Update animation duration ------------- */
function scheduleUpdate() {
  // cancel any previous work
  if (updateTimer) clearTimeout(updateTimer);
  if (removeTimer) clearTimeout(removeTimer);

  // debounce – let the browser finish the DOM changes
  updateTimer = setTimeout(() => {
    const caret = editor.querySelector('.highlight-line');
    if (!caret) return;          // nothing to do

    // how far does the caret have to move?
    const containerRect = editor.getBoundingClientRect();
    const caretRect     = caret.getBoundingClientRect();
    const emptySpace    = containerRect.right - caretRect.left - caretRect.width;

    const duration = emptySpace * 3; // same factor as before
    caret.style.animationDuration = `${duration}ms`;

    /* remove it *after* the animation completes */
    removeTimer = setTimeout(() => {
      if (!caret) return;
      caret.outerHTML = caret.innerHTML; // strip the <span>
      removeTimer = null;
    }, duration + 20);                 // a bit of wiggle room
  }, 0);
}

/* -------------  Resize handling ------------- */
function onResize() {
  const caret = editor.querySelector('.highlight-line');
  if (!caret) return;   // nothing to update

  // recompute the distance only – no timers needed
  const containerRect = editor.getBoundingClientRect();
  const caretRect     = caret.getBoundingClientRect();
  const emptySpace    = containerRect.right - caretRect.left - caretRect.width;
  const duration = emptySpace * 3;
  caret.style.animationDuration = `${duration}ms`;
}

/* -------------  Event listeners ------------- */
editor.addEventListener('keydown', e => {
  if (e.key === 'Enter') {
    e.preventDefault();     // suppress the normal <br> insertion
    insertLine();
  }
});

window.addEventListener('resize', onResize);
```

---

## 4️⃣ Why this works

| Issue | Fix |
|-------|-----|
| **Many timers → blocks accumulate** | `updateTimer` and `removeTimer` are cleared *before* scheduling a new one.  Only one caret animation can exist at a time. |
| **Caret invisible / wrong animation** | The caret is an inline‑block element that never changes width.  Its `animation-duration` is calculated from the *actual* remaining space, so it always "jumps" to the right edge. |
| **Empty space under the editor** | No extra `<br>` or empty text node is inserted after the caret; we simply place the caret after a single `<br>` that belongs to the line break.  The caret itself occupies no extra height. |
| **`highlightedLine is null` on resize** | `onResize` checks for a caret first; `removeTimer` is only scheduled if a caret exists.  `onAnimationEnd` is removed – we use a plain `setTimeout` that runs *after* the animation ends. |
| **Rapid typing** | The debounce (`setTimeout(...,0)`) gives the browser a chance to finish DOM updates before we read layout properties.  This prevents the calculation from being made on a partially updated layout. |

