## 🔒 Security Checklist (What You Already Have, What You Still Need)

| ✅ | Feature | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| ✔︎ | **Password hashing** (`bcrypt`) | 12 rounds – adjust per your CPU budget. |
| ✔︎ | **JWT signing & verification** | Keep secret in env. Use `HS256`. |
| ✔︎ | **HTTPS** | Add at reverse‑proxy level (NGINX, Cloudflare, etc.). |
| ✔︎ | **Helmet** | Sets safe HTTP headers. |
| ✔︎ | **CORS whitelist** | Protect against accidental data leaks. |
| ✔︎ | **Rate limiting** | Mitigates brute‑force attacks. |
| ✔︎ | **Input validation** (`express-validator`) | Guard against malformed data. |
| ✔︎ | **Environment variables** | Store secrets out of code. |
| ❌ | **Token revocation / rotation** | Use a short expiry + refresh token flow. |
| ❌ | **HTTPS only** | Force `Secure` & `HttpOnly` cookies if you switch to cookie‑based auth. |
| ❌ | **Audit logs** | Log authentication failures, password changes. |
| ❌ | **Account lockout** | Temporarily block after N failures. |
| ❌ | **Password reset** | Secure token + email flow. |
| ❌ | **CSRF protection** | Not needed for pure JWT‑header auth but consider for cookie‑based. |
| ❌ | **Content‑Security‑Policy** | Add `helmet` directives. |
| ❌ | **Logging / monitoring** | Use Winston + Sentry or similar. |

