Below is a **production‑ready, security‑first** refactor of your weather‑proxy endpoint.  
It keeps the same public API (`POST /weather`) but adds:

| What | Why it matters |
|------|----------------|
| **Strict input validation** | Prevents malformed or malicious payloads from flooding the downstream API. |
| **Rate‑limiting & request‑bottleneck** | Stops abuse (e.g., DDoS) and respects the RapidAPI rate‑limits. |
| **Helmet & CORS whitelisting** | Harden HTTP headers & only allow trusted origins. |
| **Axios instance + timeout + retry** | Guarantees a fast fail‑over and avoids hanging requests. |
| **In‑memory caching (LRU)** | Cuts duplicate external calls & saves quota. |
| **Environment‑variable sanity check** | Fails fast if required config is missing. |
| **Structured logging (Winston)** | Easier ops & auditability. |
| **Graceful error handling** | No leaking of stack traces, consistent status codes. |

> **Tip** – In a real deployment you’d replace the LRU cache with a distributed store (Redis, Memcached) so all nodes share results.

