> **Explanation of key security measures:**

| Section | Security Feature | Why it matters |
|---------|-----------------|----------------|
| `htmlEscape()` | Escapes all user‑controlled text before inserting into the DOM. | Prevents XSS even if the JSON file were compromised. |
| `sanitizeURL()` | Validates that all media URLs are either absolute HTTPS or relative paths. | Stops the app from loading `javascript:` or other malicious URLs. |
| CSP | (Set on the server via `Content-Security-Policy` header). | Stops inline scripts, restricts allowed origins, mitigates XSS. |
| `localStorage` handling | Minimal “encryption” (XOR + Base64) + clear‑text only minimal data. | Makes it harder for casual snooping but acknowledges that the data is client‑side only. |
| `no-store` in fetch | Forces a fresh copy of data every request; prevents caching of stale or tampered data. | Helps if you have a caching layer that could serve old data. |
| `novalidate` on form | We handle validation ourselves, ensuring that we *never* trust the browser’s native validation for malicious input. | Allows us to control sanitization. |

