## 6. README.md (optional – explains usage)

```markdown
# Blogging Tool

A lightweight, self‑hosted blogging platform built with Express, EJS, SQLite, and Bootstrap.  
Author and reader interfaces are fully separated, and all data is stored in a single SQLite database.

## Install & Run

```bash
git clone <repo-url>
cd blog
npm install
npm run build-db
npm start
```

Open `http://localhost:3000/` to see the reader front‑page.  
The author dashboard is at `http://localhost:3000/author`.

No database migrations or environment variables are required – everything is self‑contained.

## Features

- Author can create, edit, publish, and delete articles.
- Author settings (title, subtitle, name) editable.
- Reader can view published articles, like them, and add comments.
- Bootstrap 5 UI, clean and responsive.
- SQLite for persistence; all data lives in `db/blog.db`.

Happy blogging! 🎉
```

