    if (!errors.isEmpty()) return res.status(400).json({ errors: errors.array() });

    // ... controller logic ...
  });
```

---

## 5. Error Handling

| Issue | Why it matters | Recommendation |
|-------|----------------|----------------|
| **`app.use(err => { logger.error(err.stack); ... })`** | Logging the entire stack can expose stack traces in logs that attackers can read. | Filter out stack traces for production logs; log only message + sanitized request info. |
| **No 404 handler** | Missing routes return default Express 404 (which may expose request details). | Add a custom 404 middleware. |
| **Error responses always `Internal Server Error`** | Good for hiding details, but you might want to differentiate between client vs. server errors. | Use `http-errors` to generate proper error types. |

**Suggested snippet:**
```js
// 404
app.use((req, res) => {
  res.status(404).json({ error: 'Not Found' });
});

// Error handling
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  logger.warn(`Error: ${err.message}`, { request: { method: req.method, url: req.originalUrl } });

  if (err.status && err.status < 500) {
    res.status(err.status).json({ error: err.message });
  } else {
    // In production, don’t leak stack
    res.status(500).json({ error: 'Internal Server Error' });
  }
});
```

