## 2.  Server side – Safely write to a plain text file

> **Why you can’t do this on the client side**  
> Browsers are sandboxed – a web page cannot write to a file on the *server*’s filesystem.  
> The only way to persist data on the server is via an HTTP request to a backend that has file‑system access.

Below is a minimal Node.js/Express example.  
If you’re on a different stack (PHP, Python, Go…) the same ideas apply – just adjust the syntax.

### 2.1  Directory structure

```
