### 3.1 Security Highlights

| Issue | Mitigation |
|-------|------------|
| **No `eval()`** | We parse the expression manually (shunting‑yard algorithm). |
| **XSS Prevention** | All user input is treated as plain text; results are inserted via `textContent` (not `innerHTML`). |
| **CSP** | The page sets a minimal CSP header (`default-src 'self'`) to disallow inline scripts. |
| **Rate‑Limiting** | A simple time‑based debounce prevents rapid repeated calculations. |
| **Input Length** | Reject expressions > 200 characters. |
| **Error Handling** | Graceful messages, no stack traces exposed. |

