The colour is chosen from a small palette of safe, non‑jarring colours so you can see the effect quickly.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Click‑to‑Change‑Background Demo</title>
<style>
    html, body {
        height: 100%;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        /* Default background */
        background: #f0f0f0;
        /* Smooth colour transition */
        transition: background-color 0.5s ease;
        /* Center text */
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
    }
</style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Click anywhere to change the background colour</h1>

<script>
    // List of colours that will be cycled through
    const colours = [
        '#FFCDD2', // light red
        '#F8BBD0', // light pink
        '#E1BEE7', // light purple
        '#D1C4E9', // light deep purple
        '#C5CAE9', // light indigo
        '#BBDEFB', // light blue
        '#B3E5FC', // light light blue
        '#B2EBF2', // light teal
        '#B2DFDB', // light green
        '#C8E6C9', // light light green
        '#DCEDC8', // light lime
        '#F0F4C3', // light yellow
        '#FFF9C4', // light amber
        '#FFE0B2', // light orange
        '#FFCCBC', // light deep orange
        '#D7CCC8', // light brown
        '#F5F5F5', // light grey
        '#EEEEEE', // grey
        '#BDBDBD', // dark grey
    ];

    let idx = 0; // current index in the colour array

    document.body.addEventListener('click', function () {
        // Advance to next colour, wrap around at the end
        idx = (idx + 1) % colours.length;
        document.body.style.backgroundColor = colours[idx];
    });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

1. **HTML & CSS** – The page is a full‑screen flex container with a default light grey background and a transition defined so that background colour changes fade smoothly.
2. **Colour palette** – `colours` is an array of hex codes. You can add, remove or reorder colours as you wish.
3. **Event listener** – The script attaches a `click` handler to the `<body>`. Each click increments an index and sets the body's background colour to the next colour in the array.
4. **Wrap‑around** – When the array’s end is reached, the index wraps back to the first colour.

Feel free to paste this code into a file (e.g., `click-change-bg.html`) and open it in a browser to see the effect in action.

