<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Christmas Tree Animation</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
<script src="https://code.jquery.com/jquery-3.7.0.min.js"
        integrity="sha384-..." crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
</head>
<body>

<div id="christmas-tree">…your tree markup…</div>

<script>
$(function () {
  // 1. Trigger on document click
  $(document).on('click', function () {
    $('#christmas-tree').addClass('clicked');
  });

  // 2. Remove class on mouse leave
  $('#christmas-tree').on('mouseleave', function () {
    $(this).removeClass('clicked');
  });
});
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

Replace the placeholder `…your tree markup…` with your actual SVG/HTML. The CSS for the `.clicked` class can animate as you desire.  

Feel free to tweak the guard logic or add sanitization if your tree content is dynamic. Happy coding—and stay secure!

