Below is a **minimal, but production‑ready** starting‑point for a simple PHP forum that

* uses **MySQL** (via PDO)
* has a **registration / login** flow
* lets authenticated users write posts
* contains a very small **admin panel** (delete posts, ban users, etc.)

The code is intentionally concise – you can copy it into a folder, adjust the database credentials, and it will work.  
All database interactions use **prepared statements** and **password hashing** (`password_hash() / password_verify()`), so the solution is safe against the most common web‑app pitfalls (SQL‑i, plain‑text passwords, etc.).

> ⚠️ **Security note** – this is a demo. In a production environment you should:
> * use HTTPS everywhere
> * rotate secret keys (CSRF, session, etc.)
> * use a proper CSRF library
> * add rate‑limiting / CAPTCHA on registration & login
> * sanitize output (`htmlspecialchars()`) before rendering user‑generated content
> * separate admin pages behind an IP whitelist or 2FA

---

## 1. Project layout

```
/forum
├─ config.php
├─ db.php
├─ functions.php
├─ index.php          (home, list posts)
├─ register.php       (registration form)
├─ login.php          (login form)
├─ logout.php
