| **link daftar** | URL to the brand’s registration page | `<a href="$linkDaftar">Daftar</a>` |
| **main banner** | URL to a full‑width banner image | `<img src="$mainBanner">` |

Below you’ll find two code samples:

1. **The “client” code** – the page that receives the `daftar` GET parameter, validates the brand, then asks a **remote API** for the three URLs.  
2. **The “remote API”** – a tiny JSON‑returning endpoint that the client talks to.  It simply looks up the brand in a server‑side array (or DB) and spits out the URLs.

> **⚠️ Security note** –  
>  • Treat the remote endpoint like any other external service: verify the TLS cert, avoid `allow_url_fopen` if possible, and never trust the payload without validation.  
>  • Use `cURL` (or the modern `Guzzle`/`Symfony HTTP Client`) with `CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYHOST` & `CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYPEER` enabled.  
>  • Escape all output (`htmlspecialchars`, `urlencode`, etc.) to prevent XSS.  
>  • If you need to restrict which domains may call the API, consider an API key or a short‑lived JWT.  

---

## 1. Client Side (Your Main Domain)

```php
