## 3.  `Classes/Quiz.php`

```php
<?php
/**
 * Handles the collection of questions, rendering and scoring.
 */
class Quiz
{
    /** @var Question[] */
    private array $questions = [];

    /** Add a question instance */
    public function addQuestion(Question $q): void
    {
        $this->questions[$q->getUuid()] = $q;
    }

    /** Render the whole form */
    public function afficheQuiz(): void
    {
        echo '<form method="post" action="Action/submit.php">';
        foreach ($this->questions as $q) {
            $q->afficheQuestion();
            echo '<br>';
        }
        echo '<input type="submit" name="submit" value="Valider">';
        echo '</form>';
    }

    /** Score the answers sent by the form */
    public function checkReponse(array $post): int
    {
        $score = 0;
        foreach ($this->questions as $uuid => $question) {
            if (isset($post[$uuid])) {
                // we cast to string because some inputs may be int etc.
                $userAnswer = (string) $post[$uuid];
                if ($question->checkReponse($userAnswer)) {
                    $score++;
                }
            }
        }
        return $score;
    }

    /** Needed for rebuild in submit.php */
    public function getUuidList(): array
    {
        return array_keys($this->questions);
    }

    /** For re‑building the quiz in submit.php */
    public function getQuestionsData(): array
    {
        $data = [];
        foreach ($this->questions as $q) {
            $data[] = $q->getData(); // we add a helper in Question
        }
        return $data;
    }
}
```

*Why this works*

* The `Quiz` only knows the **interface** of a question, not how it is implemented.
* It keeps questions in an associative array keyed by their `uuid` so the form fields
  are unique.
* `checkReponse()` loops through all questions and uses the concrete implementation
  of each.

