## 5.  Security Checklist

| Item | Why it matters | How to do it |
|------|----------------|--------------|
| **HTTPS** | Protects data in transit, including passwords. | Obtain an SSL certificate (Let’s Encrypt, etc.). |
| **Strong password policy** | Forces users to choose more secure passwords. | Min length, complexity, maybe password‑strength meter. |
| **Password hashing** | Never store raw passwords. | Use `password_hash()`/`password_verify()`. |
| **Prepared statements** | Prevents SQL injection. | PDO with bound parameters. |
| **Rate limiting / account lockout** | Stops brute‑force attempts. | Store `failed_logins` & `lock_until`. |
| **CSRF tokens** | Stops cross‑site request forgery. | Generate a token per form, store in session, verify on POST. |
