## 6. cleanup.php (cron job)

```php
<?php
require_once 'config.php';

// Delete files whose expiry time has passed
$now = time();
$stmt = $pdo->prepare("SELECT id, stored_name FROM files WHERE expiry_time > 0 AND expiry_time < :now");
$stmt->execute([':now' => $now]);

$toDelete = [];
while ($row = $stmt->fetch(PDO::FETCH_ASSOC)) {
    $filePath = __DIR__ . '/uploads/' . $row['stored_name'];
    if (file_exists($filePath)) {
        @unlink($filePath);
    }
    $toDelete[] = $row['id'];
}

// Delete DB rows
if ($toDelete) {
    $in  = str_repeat('?,', count($toDelete) - 1) . '?';
    $stmt = $pdo->prepare("DELETE FROM files WHERE id IN ($in)");
    $stmt->execute($toDelete);
}

echo count($toDelete) . " expired files removed.\n";
```

> Set this script to run every day (or hourly) via cron:
> ```
> 0 0 * * * /usr/bin/php /path/to/filehost/cleanup.php
> ```

