## 2. Admin Web Interface – CRUD

Below is a **minimal, secure, and easy‑to‑extend** implementation using **PHP 8.1+**, **PDO**, and **Bootstrap 5**.  
(You can translate the same ideas to another language/framework – e.g. Django, Laravel, Express/Node, Flask, etc.)

> **Security notes**  
> * All database access uses prepared statements (protects against SQL injection).  
> * CSRF protection via a signed token stored in session and verified on POST.  
> * All output is HTML‑escaped (`htmlspecialchars`) to mitigate XSS.  
> * Authentication is represented by a simple session flag – replace it with a real auth system (OAuth, JWT, etc.).  
> * Use HTTPS in production.  
> * Keep the database user to the minimum required privileges (e.g. only SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE on `library_books`).  
> * Log all CRUD operations; consider an audit trail.

