## Quick‑start guide  
Below you will find a minimal set of PHP 8 files that you can drop into a web‑root of a PHP 8 server.  
The code talks to the **Matomo (Piwik)** HTTP API, shows the list of available sites, lets you pick a site and a date range, chooses a format (CSV / Excel / PDF) and then streams the file back for download.

> **Important security notes**  
> * Store the Matomo API token in an environment variable or a file that is **not** reachable via the web.  
> * Always use HTTPS when talking to Matomo (the code checks the SSL cert).  
> * Sanitize all user input and validate that the requested site ID and dates exist on the Matomo server.  
> * Add CSRF protection for production use (not shown in this demo).  

---

## File list

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `config.php` | Configuration (Matomo URL, token) |
| `matomo_api.php` | Thin wrapper around the Matomo HTTP API |
| `index.php` | Front‑end page that shows the site picker and date/form selectors |
| `get_sites.php` | AJAX endpoint that returns the list of sites as JSON |
| `get_report.php` | AJAX endpoint that calls Matomo and streams the chosen report |

You can keep all the files in the same folder, e.g. `/matomo-export/`.  
Create a **`.htaccess`** or server rule to block direct access to `config.php` if you are on Apache/Nginx.

---

## 1️⃣ config.php

```php
<?php
/**
 * config.php
 * ------------------------------------------------------------------
 * Store Matomo credentials and general settings here.
 * This file should NOT be served by the web server.
 */

declare(strict_types=1);

return [
    // Base URL of your Matomo instance (must end with /index.php/)
    'matomo_url' => 'https://your-matomo.example.com/matomo.php',

    // API token for a user that has read access to all sites you need
    // Put the token in an environment variable or a .env file for safety
    'auth_token' => getenv('MATOMO_API_TOKEN'),

    // Optional: timeout for the HTTP requests (seconds)
    'http_timeout' => 30,
];
```

> **Tip:** In production you can use a package like `vlucas/phpdotenv` to load the token from a `.env` file.

---

## 2️⃣ matomo_api.php

```php
<?php
/**
 * matomo_api.php
 * ------------------------------------------------------------------
 * Very small helper that talks to the Matomo API.
 * It uses the built‑in cURL extension.
 */

declare(strict_types=1);

class MatomoApi
{
    private string $baseUrl;
    private string $token;
    private int $timeout;

    public function __construct(array $config)
    {
        $this->baseUrl = rtrim($config['matomo_url'], '/');
        $this->token   = $config['auth_token'];
        $this->timeout = $config['http_timeout'] ?? 30;
    }

    /**
     * @param string $method   Matomo API method name (e.g. 'SitesManager.getSitesWithAdminAccess')
     * @param array  $params   Additional query parameters
     *
     * @return array  Parsed JSON response
     * @throws RuntimeException on HTTP or parsing error
     */
    public function call(string $method, array $params = []): array
    {
        $query = array_merge(
            ['module' => 'API', 'method' => $method, 'format' => 'JSON', 'token_auth' => $this->token],
            $params
        );

        $url = $this->baseUrl . '?' . http_build_query($query);

        $ch = curl_init($url);
        curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_RETURNTRANSFER, true);
        curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_TIMEOUT, $this->timeout);
        curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_FOLLOWLOCATION, true);
        curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYPEER, true);
        curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYHOST, 2);

        $response = curl_exec($ch);
        if ($response === false) {
            throw new RuntimeException('cURL error: ' . curl_error($ch));
        }

        $httpCode = curl_getinfo($ch, CURLINFO_HTTP_CODE);
        curl_close($ch);

        if ($httpCode !== 200) {
            throw new RuntimeException("Matomo API returned HTTP {$httpCode}");
        }

        $decoded = json_decode($response, true, 512, JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR);
        return $decoded;
    }
}
```

---

## 3️⃣ index.php

